A||N||7||V8Dreamer||Jumping out the AC compressor???||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||06-18-2001||11:49 AM||||When I picked up my R-134a kit, the guy at the advance auto said something to me about possibly having to "jump out" the compressor to get the clutch to engage if the system is completely out of R-12......Has anyone heard of this before, and if so can someone let me know how it can be done?  I'm assuming that he meant I needed to bypass a cutoff switch or something that is meant to save the compressor from self destruction.<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||LAMBO||06-18-2001||01:11 PM||||.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LAMBO (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||06-18-2001||01:25 PM||||Why would you want to do this?  Aren't you supposed to have evacuated all the R-12 and water from the system first?  This means the system is under about 29" vacuum and the A/C compressor won't engage.  <P>You don't need the clutch engaged to put the first can of R-134 in, it will get sucked in on its own.  You then add the oil (at least that's what I remember from the Interdynamics kits I've installed).Then there should be enough pressure in the system to engage the clutch so the last can or so of R-134 can be installed.<P>Good luck...||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||06-18-2001||05:27 PM||||Yes, that is correct. I just did one, My 3rd system fill/conversion. <P>1. Start car AC on High.<BR>2. Add 1 can R-134a can upside down. <BR>3. shake oil can then add upside down. <BR>4. Clutch should have kick in by now. <BR>5. Add next R-134 can upside down half way than right side up. <BR>6. If you still need more after doing the math than add some from last can. I use a pressure gauge to tell how much to add. I bring the High side to 225-250 cycle at 275 bringing the front to 35-40 to activate the pressure switch which may need adjusting by the screw centered under the plug when it is removed to get the correct cycling.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadaver||06-18-2001||09:46 PM||||But why not just fill it with R-12?||||reg||1
Z||000005||V8Dreamer||06-18-2001||10:13 PM||||Well,<P>since I grabbed the wrong AC lines at the boneyard, I won't be adding ANY R-134a anytime soon....that is not until I find out where I can get the correct lines for an 86 2m4 cheap.  Any suggestions??  My original one is completely broken off right next to the compressor.<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000006||Chris McDonald||06-19-2001||11:30 AM||||What he means by "jumping" the compressor is very simple.  On the low pressure switch on the drier there is a wire harness with two wires in it.  When the pressure meets or exceeds a certain amount (see prior post-it is adjustable with a small screwdriver) it will then close the circuit and the clutch will engage.  <P>If the clutch does not engage after you have added the first can (while the system is off).  Crank up the car, take a jumper wire and use it to close the circuit on the low pressure switch (connect the two wires).  This will force the clutch to engage and allow the system to suck in the remaining charge.  When you have a full charge, you can plug the harness back on the low pressure switch and it should cycle as needed.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||06-19-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>But why not just fill it with R-12?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Because #1 cost. When I was going to tech school They supplied it free but, It costs $100's #2 Most people don't have the certification to buy it. 100 Question booklet. #3 they don't have it in the little cans, You must have lots of equipment to use it.<P>I will stick with the $30 kits.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
